60
00:07:20,555 --> 00:07:21,535
[SPEAKER_00]: What would be its purpose?

61
00:07:21,595 --> 00:07:24,896
[SPEAKER_00]: And who kind of would oversee kind of management budget of it?

62
00:07:26,553 --> 00:07:33,957
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, the tree fund is actually defined in this, and so I'll just read it for folks who may be listening in.

63
00:07:34,758 --> 00:07:41,442
[SPEAKER_01]: An account established pursuant to this ordinance for the deposit of payments for mitigating tree removal in lieu of tree replanting.

64
00:07:42,022 --> 00:07:51,628
[SPEAKER_01]: This fund may only be expended as a means of promoting a healthy tree canopy and will be applied to the cost of site preparation, tree replanting, and new tree maintenance.

65
00:07:54,802 --> 00:07:57,063
[SPEAKER_01]: So do you mind re-asking your question?

66
00:07:57,103 --> 00:07:57,583
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, sure.

67
00:07:57,663 --> 00:08:04,105
[SPEAKER_00]: So is this something that's like, is the oversight by DPW, is it oversight by the tree warden?

68
00:08:05,105 --> 00:08:12,028
[SPEAKER_00]: Where would the budget or what would that look like in terms of what the needs might be for utilizing this type of fund?

69
00:08:13,748 --> 00:08:15,429
[SPEAKER_00]: That is such a great question.

70
00:08:15,449 --> 00:08:35,999
[SPEAKER_01]: I will admit to being like these a lot of this has been so long in and out of committee and so let me see if I can find some information on that or I don't know if the counselors have been here longer than I have because this was originally you know something from

