90
00:09:38,992 --> 00:09:50,838
[SPEAKER_02]: So the first one being, this compensation shall be calculated by measuring the canopy cover using recent aerial photography, such as Google Maps coverage or aerial photography.

91
00:09:52,858 --> 00:09:57,440
[SPEAKER_02]: Actually, I feel like the second aerial photography is a little redundant.

92
00:09:57,741 --> 00:09:58,901
[SPEAKER_02]: I agree.

93
00:09:59,041 --> 00:09:59,722
[SPEAKER_02]: Reading out loud.

94
00:09:59,862 --> 00:10:04,605
[SPEAKER_02]: We're using recent aerial photography such as Google Maps coverage or aerial photography.

95
00:10:06,627 --> 00:10:25,717
[SPEAKER_02]: actually it's I feel like that the second aerial photography is a little redundant replacement trees at the current rate and salaries and costs for staff time for selecting watering and monitoring those trees so that would be that phrasing is for just however however many trees are used to replace it the second phrasing I have

96
00:10:27,137 --> 00:10:31,361
[SPEAKER_02]: is based on canopy coverage.

97
00:10:32,222 --> 00:10:34,143
[SPEAKER_02]: So it'd be likely a higher number.

98
00:10:35,685 --> 00:10:47,455
[SPEAKER_02]: This compensation shall be calculated by measuring the canopy cover using recent aerial photography, such as Google Maps coverage, determining the number of young trees that would have the equivalent canopy coverage.

99
00:10:48,249 --> 00:10:59,686
[SPEAKER_02]: the fine shall be the sum of the cost of preparing the site, planting that number of trees at the current contract rate and salaries and costs for staff time for selecting.

